{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Cloud Stream binders for migrated modules to ensure compatibility with the existing ecosystem.",
    "Implement module upload via REST API using Spring's multipart file upload support and shell integration via Spring Shell.",
    "Replace the hard-coded module registry with a dynamic registry backed by a file system or database for immediate updates.",
    "Leverage Spring Boot auto-configuration for migrated modules to minimize boilerplate code.",
    "Use Java 17+ features (e.g., records, pattern matching) for new code to align with Spring Framework 6.0 requirements."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All modules (jms, mail, mongo, mqtt, reactor-ip, stdout) can be migrated with minimal code changes, primarily adjusting dependencies and configurations.",
    "The module registry will use a file-based storage system for simplicity, with modules stored in a predefined directory.",
    "Existing unit and integration tests for Spring XD modules can be adapted for the migrated modules with minor modifications.",
    "The shell and REST API will share a common backend service for module upload to avoid duplication.",
    "Documentation updates will focus on new features and module migration guides, assuming existing documentation covers base functionality."
  ],
  "activities": [
